    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Table&nbsp;5.01</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Retinoblastoma subtypes (genetic and histological features)</span></p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Patricia Chevez-Barrios",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 485.75pt; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"648\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.85pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">General type</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.85pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Subtype</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 252.05pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"336\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Definition</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"4\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Genetic</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Sporadic (H0)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 252.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"336\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No history of hereditary retinoblastoma; patient without a germline <em>RB1</em> mutation (normal <em>RB1</em> alleles in blood, high-sensitivity assays)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Normal <em>RB1</em> in blood, &lt;&nbsp;1% risk of mosaicism <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{20301625}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.85pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Hereditary (H1)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 252.05pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"336\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Bilateral retinoblastoma with or without intracranial CNS midline embryonic tumour (i.e. trilateral retinoblastoma); family history of retinoblastoma or molecular definition of germline <em>RB1</em> gene mutation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Unknown (HX)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 252.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"336\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Unknown <em>RB1</em> mutation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.85pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">MYCN</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> amplified</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 252.05pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"336\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">High-level amplification of the <em>MYCN</em> gene (approximately &gt;&nbsp;28&nbsp;copies) with no detectable mutation in <em>RB1</em></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.85pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"4\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Histopathology</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Growth patterns</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 252.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"336\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Exophytic, endophytic, combined exophytic and endophytic, diffuse, diffuse anterior, indeterminate, extensively necrotic (&gt;&nbsp;90%)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.85pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Degree of differentiation (grade) <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">[[Milman T, Grossniklaus HE, Eagle RC Jr, et al. Protocol for the Examination of Specimens from Patients with Retinoblastoma. Version: Retinoblastoma 4.1.0.0. Northfield (IL): College of American Pathologists; 2021 Jun. Available from: https://www.cap.org/protocols-and-guidelines/cancer-reporting-tools/cancer-protocol-templates.]]</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 252.05pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"336\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">1.&nbsp;Areas of retinocytoma (fleurettes&nbsp;/ neuronal differentiation)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">2.&nbsp;Many rosettes (Flexner&ndash;Wintersteiner or Homer Wright)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">3.&nbsp;Occasional rosettes</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">4.&nbsp;Poorly differentiated cells without rosettes and/or &gt;&nbsp;50% anaplasia</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">RB1</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> mutated&nbsp;/ conventional</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 252.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"336\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Neuroendocrine type, irregular nuclei, without nucleoli, with rosettes</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.85pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">MYCN</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> amplified</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 252.05pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"336\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Unilateral retinoblastoma with round nuclei and prominent nucleoli without rosettes</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
